<title>USA: Atchison Casting unit gets order.</title>
<headline>Atchison Casting unit gets order.</headline>
<dateline>ATCHISON, Kan. 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atchison Casting Corp said Monday its Montreal-based Canadian Steel Foundries Ltd unit received casting orders for hydroelectric projects in Turkey and China valued at more than $3.0 million.</p>
<p>Orders were received from Sulzer Hydro GmbH of Ravensburg, Germany.</p>
<p>The statement did not specify the location of the hydroelectric projects in Turkey and China.</p>
<p>Atchison Casting produces iron, steel and non-ferrous castings.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
